  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "How to read this page",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 3
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**Every backup job in one table: what it protects, where the copy lives, and how fresh it is.** Status is the age of the newest good copy against what that job is allowed: **OK** (under 70%) \u00b7 **AGING** (70-100%) \u00b7 **OVERDUE** (past its allowed age, an alert is raised) \u00b7 **NO DATA** (nothing reported at all). A failed or overdue backup sends a phone notice between 07:00 and 22:00 and nothing overnight (the 08:00 summary lists it too). Below the table: what is covered by what, which guests are in no job, the live alerts, and space on the backup targets."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Backup status",
   "description": "Jobs past their allowed age or with nothing reported. Zero = every tracked job is within its limit.",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 3,
    "w": 4,
    "h": 4
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count(rl:backup_job_age_ratio >= 1) or vector(0)",
     "refId": "A",
     "instant": true,
     "range": false
    }
   ],
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "suffix: overdue",
     "mappings": [
      {
       "type": "value",
       "options": {
        "0": {
         "text": "ALL OK",
         "color": "green",
         "index": 0
