  {
   "id": 23,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "When you hear about it",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 12,
    "y": 60,
    "w": 12,
    "h": 8
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "A failed or overdue backup sends a phone notice between **07:00 and 22:00**, repeated every 6 hours until fixed. Nothing overnight: a problem found at night goes out when the window opens at 07:00 (and is in the 08:00 summary).\n\n| Alert | Raised when |\n|---|---|\n| *BackupJobFailed* | the last Proxmox backup run reported errors (about 10 minutes after the run) |\n| *BackupMissing / NeverRan* | a guest has no good copy within the job's allowed age (30 h NAS, 17 d off-site) |\n| *HyperBackupStale* | no Hyper Backup commit for 26 h (daily tasks) |\n| *NodeBackupFailed / Stale* | a node's nightly backup failed (10 min) or none for 27 h |\n| *BackupArtifactStale* | Home Assistant, FreePBX, ChannelsDVR, a node's file on the NAS, or the Paperless export is older than its limit |\n| *...CollectorStale* | a checker stopped reporting, so its alerts are blind |\n\nJob limits live next to each backup: Proxmox in `pve-backup-metrics.py`, files in Ansible `monitoring_backup_artifacts`."
   }
  },
